overloads.raises_doc:
The predicate's or body's exact error type. Their errors must match,
including origins, or one must be `Never`. Failure stops immediately;
receiver updates are retained and the current carry is destroyed.

get_or.description:
Both the Result and the default are consumed. On Ok, the unused default
is destroyed. Argument expressions evaluate normally before this call;
use `get_or_else(factory)` to construct a default only on Err.

effects.IO.description:
Use delay, pure[IO[E]], map, flat_map and tail_rec_m to construct recipes;
run_io consumes one at the host boundary. Native callbacks run synchronously.
Cancellation uses the outer Optional and cannot be recovered as a stored error.

effects.Listen.description:
The payload becomes (value, log). Only the supplied computation is observed;
surrounding writes remain outside that observation. Listening requires a
copyable log, but the dictionary may still support tell for move-only logs.

overloads.description:
The output log is retained. Only the supplied computation's log is observed;
surrounding writes and other Writer layers are unchanged. Generic forwarders
retain ListenCompatible, including log copyability and carrier origins.

drop_while.description:
Construction pulls nothing. Take consumes the first rejected candidate;
drop yields it and stops testing. Bounds and exhaustion remain native.
Use the value-taking overload for an owned closure or library predicate.

filter.description:
The predicate borrows each candidate. Rejected elements are destroyed;
accepted elements are moved out unchanged. Plain functions, closures and
non-raising `BorrowCallable` values are supported.

filter_not.description:
Calls run only as elements are pulled. Each candidate is borrowed once;
retained values move unchanged. Plain functions, stored closures and
non-raising BorrowCallable values are supported, as with filter.

take_while.description:
Construction pulls nothing. Take consumes the first rejected candidate;
drop yields it and stops testing. Bounds and exhaustion remain native.
Use the value-taking overload for an owned closure or library predicate.
